%% The Administrator starts the calculation; the settlement engine computes it (UC38). Customer refunds are settled before the Pool is computed.
%% Connector A continues on part 2. Investor and Operator review in parallel; the merge joins the two outcomes of the Investor's branch before the join.
%% Feedback moves the settlement to Disputed until the Administrator answers it (Figure 4.15). Connector B continues on part 3. Approval locks the
%% statement and creates one payment instruction per payee (Figure 4.12); the sandbox gateway answers at once (Created → Succeeded or Failed). The last
%% successful payout closes the settlement and the Batch. Traceability: UC38, UC37, UC35, UC36, UC39, UC40 (TP1 Thiện). Worked example (Register v1.4):
%% Standard Cost 100,000,000 VND; revenue 300,000,000 VND → Pool 200,000,000 VND; survival 90% above an 85% threshold → remuneration 10% = 20,000,000
%% VND; A receives 15,000,000 + 27,000,000 = 42,000,000 VND, B the same, C 196,000,000 VND, so payouts plus remuneration equal the revenue; at 80%
%% survival the remuneration halves. Exception branches: negative Revenue Pool (loss capped at capital, no capital call, no carry-over), recalculation,
%% investor feedback, failed payout resent. «planned» in v1.4: revenue lines InvoicedSale (low-grade or resold crabs), ForfeitedDeposit and FinalOrder
%% (the code counts completed orders and offtake forfeits), remuneration tiers by survival rate (the code uses one fixed percentage). Survival = 1 −
%% deaths ÷ crabs stocked in the funded boxes; restocked crabs that die count, deaths in transit only lower revenue. Unused Standard Cost, including an
%% unused mortality reserve, stays with the Operator; only an early liquidation returns unspent capital. Removed in v1.4 (still in code): offtake
%% forfeits as revenue. States: settlement Draft → Proposed ⇄ Disputed → Approved → PaidOut → Closed (Figure 4.14); payment instruction Created →
%% Succeeded / Failed (4.12); Batch Settlement → Closed (4.8). Design decisions of 05/11/2026 applied here were confirmed by the lead.
